; ===============================================================
;  Quad field-error tolerance study
;  Same FODO as quad_alignment_tolerance, but the random draws are
;  on the *gradient* and on the parsed-but-historically-ignored
;  g3 (sextupole) and g4 (octupole) multipole content.
;
;  The Quadrupole element now actually applies g3/g4 (since
;  2026-05-08), so this directive directly probes the optical
;  sensitivity to power-supply jitter and end-field nonlinearities.
; ===============================================================
TITLE Quad field-error tolerance
FREQ 325
PARTRAN_STEP 100 50
;
; --- Field-error directive: applies to the next 8 QUADs ---
;     N  r  dx dy φx φy φz   dG  dG3  dG4 dG5 dG6
;                        gradient: σ = 1 %
;                                       g3:   σ = 5 %
;                                            g4:   σ = 2 %
ERROR_QUAD_NCPL_STAT 8 2 0  0  0  0  0   1   5   2   0   0
;
DRIFT 100 20
QUAD 100 8 20 0 0.05 0.01 0 0 0    ; quad with non-zero g3, g4 design value
DRIFT 250 20
QUAD 100 -8 20 0 0.05 0.01 0 0 0
DRIFT 250 20
QUAD 100 8 20 0 0.05 0.01 0 0 0
DRIFT 250 20
QUAD 100 -8 20 0 0.05 0.01 0 0 0
DRIFT 250 20
QUAD 100 8 20 0 0.05 0.01 0 0 0
DRIFT 250 20
QUAD 100 -8 20 0 0.05 0.01 0 0 0
DRIFT 250 20
QUAD 100 8 20 0 0.05 0.01 0 0 0
DRIFT 250 20
QUAD 100 -8 20 0 0.05 0.01 0 0 0
DRIFT 200 20
END
